## Validation evidence

- UNCONFIRMED: commands run before review freeze.
- UNCONFIRMED: known failures and waived checks.

## Review lanes

Each reviewer works independently against the same frozen version.

- security
- architecture
- tests
- UX / visual behavior
- performance
- maintainability

## Report format

Write one JSON report per lane under `docs/reviews/pending/<lane>.json`.

```json
{
  "reviewer_lane": "security",
  "base_commit": "{{CURRENT_COMMIT}}",
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "SEC-001",
      "severity": "P1",
      "claim": "Describe the issue.",
      "evidence": {"files": ["src/example.ts:1"], "observed": "..."},
      "affected_files": ["src/example.ts"],
      "acceptance_criteria": ["Expected behavior is verified."],
      "validation_commands": ["npm test"],
      "requires_human_decision": false
    }
  ]
}
```

## Normalize feedback

After all independent reports are complete, run from the target repo:

```text
invoke $codex-longrun-kit normalize review feedback
```

Skill package owns the helper. Target repo owns generated docs.

Then fix `docs/reviews/ReviewQueue.json` tickets one at a time. HITL tickets wait for human decision.
